    ret = -EINVAL;
    goto clean_state;
}
```
Reason:
The `allocate_actors_buffer()` function checks if there are no cooling devices (indicated by `num_actors` being zero) and returns `-EINVAL`, which causes the probing of the thermal zone to fail. This is inappropriate because cooling devices can be added later, and the thermal governor should not fail due to their absence at the time of probing.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!num_actors) {
    ret = 0;
    goto clean_state;
}
```
Reason:
The patch modifies the behavior of the `allocate_actors_buffer()` function to return `0` instead of `-EINVAL` when there are no cooling devices. This change allows the probing of the thermal zone to succeed even when no cooling devices are attached, accommodating the possibility of devices being added later.

